---
import DocsShell from '../../components/docs/DocsShell.astro';
import FieldTable from '../../components/docs/FieldTable.astro';
import {
	API_BASE,
	DETAIL_FIELDS,
	EXAMPLE_DETAIL,
	EXAMPLE_PASSPORT,
	EXAMPLE_PREFLIGHT,
	EXAMPLE_SUMMARY,
	json,
	PASSPORT_FIELDS,
	PREFLIGHT_FIELDS,
	SUMMARY_FIELDS,
	VERSION_FIELDS,
} from '../../lib/api-docs';

const errors = [
	{ status: '400', when: 'Search q is missing or longer than 500 characters', error: 'q must be 1-500 characters' },
	{ status: '404', when: 'The slug is not a published skill, or the version does not exist', error: 'not found' },
	{ status: '429', when: 'More than 20 searches in a minute from one IP', error: 'Too many requests, slow down.' },
	{ status: '500', when: 'Unexpected server error', error: 'internal error' },
	{
		status: '502',
		when: 'Pre-flight could not read the stored snapshot',
		error: 'could not fetch the source snapshot; try again',
	},
	{ status: '502', when: 'Search could not embed the query', error: 'AI search is temporarily unavailable' },
	{ status: '503', when: 'AI search is not configured on the server', error: 'AI search is not configured' },
];
---

<DocsShell
	title="Public API"
	description="The SkillPass public read API: the Skill Passport JSON, list, detail, version, pre-flight, and search endpoints, response fields, errors, and rate limits. No auth required."
>
	<p>
		Everything the directory and the <a href="/docs/cli">CLI</a> show comes from a public, read-only JSON API. No
		account and no key are needed. The base URL is:
	</p>
	<pre><code>{API_BASE}</code></pre>
	<p>
		Every response is an envelope. A success carries <code>"success": true</code> and the payload in <code>data</code>;
		a failure carries <code>"success": false</code> and a message in <code>error</code>, with a matching HTTP status.
	</p>
	<pre><code>{`{ "success": true, "data": <payload> }
{ "success": false, "error": "not found" }`}</code></pre>
	<p>
		The API only answers browser requests from skillpass.dev, so another site's front end cannot call it directly. Call
		it from a server, a script, or the CLI.
	</p>

	<h2>The Skill Passport</h2>
	<p>
		The passport is the public, immutable validation record generated for each published version. It arrives as
		<code>data.passport</code> on the skill and version endpoints below. Permission keys are listed with their meanings
		in the <a href="/docs/validation">permission taxonomy</a>.
	</p>
	<FieldTable fields={PASSPORT_FIELDS} />
	<p>An example passport, from the pdf skill:</p>
	<pre><code>{json(EXAMPLE_PASSPORT)}</code></pre>

	<h2>List skills</h2>
	<pre><code>{`GET /skills

curl ${API_BASE}/skills`}</code></pre>
	<p>
		Every published skill in one array, with no pagination. Featured listings come first in their curated order, then
		everything else, newest first. Each item is a summary:
	</p>
	<FieldTable fields={SUMMARY_FIELDS} />
	<pre><code>{json({ success: true, data: [EXAMPLE_SUMMARY] })}</code></pre>

	<h2>Get a skill</h2>
	<pre><code>{`GET /skills/:slug

curl ${API_BASE}/skills/pdf`}</code></pre>
	<p>The latest published version: every summary field above, plus these. A slug that is not published returns 404.</p>
	<FieldTable fields={DETAIL_FIELDS} />
	<p>
		Each <code>versions</code> entry:
	</p>
	<FieldTable fields={VERSION_FIELDS} />
	<pre><code>{json({ success: true, data: EXAMPLE_DETAIL })}</code></pre>

	<h2>Get a pinned version</h2>
	<pre><code>{`GET /skills/:slug/:version

curl ${API_BASE}/skills/pdf/1.0.0`}</code></pre>
	<p>
		The same shape as the skill endpoint, with the version, status, risk, and passport of the requested version instead
		of the latest. An unknown version returns 404.
	</p>

	<h2>Pre-flight</h2>
	<pre><code>{`GET /skills/:slug/:version/preflight

curl ${API_BASE}/skills/pdf/1.0.0/preflight`}</code></pre>
	<p>
		The check the CLI runs before every install: the pinned verdict, the source hash re-verified against the stored
		snapshot, and the permission changes since the previous version.
	</p>
	<FieldTable fields={PREFLIGHT_FIELDS} />
	<pre><code>{json({ success: true, data: EXAMPLE_PREFLIGHT })}</code></pre>

	<h2>Search</h2>
	<pre><code>{`GET /skills/search?q=<query>

curl -G ${API_BASE}/skills/search --data-urlencode "q=fill in a PDF form"`}</code></pre>
	<p>
		Semantic search: the query is embedded and matched against every published skill. <code>q</code> must be 1 to 500
		characters. The response is the same summary array as the list endpoint, up to 20 skills ordered by similarity.
		There is no relevance cutoff, so the 20 closest skills come back even when none is a strong match.
	</p>

	<h2>Errors and rate limits</h2>
	<p>
		Of these endpoints, only search is rate limited, at 20 requests per minute per client IP. Every failure uses the
		envelope above with one of these statuses:
	</p>
	<div class="overflow-x-auto">
		<table>
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th>Status</th>
					<th>When</th>
					<th>error</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				{errors.map((row) => (
					<tr>
						<td>
							<code>{row.status}</code>
						</td>
						<td>{row.when}</td>
						<td>
							<code>{row.error}</code>
						</td>
					</tr>
				))}
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>

	<h2>Compatibility</h2>
	<p>
		New fields can appear in any response, so ignore keys you do not recognize. Fields marked optional can be missing
		entirely. Fields typed with <code>null</code> are always present but can be null.
	</p>
</DocsShell>
